A checkbox is a marker and not text, so it survives a round trip as a
checkbox rather than as escaped brackets.

Without the tasklist extension cmark reads `- [ ] text` as an item whose
text opens with a bracket. Escaping that bracket is right for text and
wrong for a box, so every task list in every document came back as
`- \[ \]` and the feature was gone.

The `then-args` pass formats the first pass again, so this case asserts
the bytes AND that a second pass changes nothing.
